 I'm okay we've  already seen a number of players break  social distancing rules and not care and  whatever else so I just would like to  get a gauge of that and then the big  question I have for you Peter just one  thing here you know without XI confident  that the testing would be so prevalent  that it would be able to be handled the  way he explained it to where you're  gonna be able to test all these players  of people in the organization multiple  times a week or every day or twice a day  Chris I asked him I said if and I put  pen to paper if you test every active  player twice a week during the season  and and and and you did that through the  course of the season you started say in  mid-august and you went until the  Superbowl it would be four essential  personnel on every team about two  hundred thousand tests and I asked him  isn't that a little piggish to suggest  that you know all teams you know that  NFL teams could use that when tests are  so minoo people are desperate for tests  in this country and he said right now it  would be but in two three four months  from now we should have enough tests  that plus the fact Chris you know Donald  Trump wants the NFL to play yeah if it  if it means if it means funneling enough  tests to NFL teams to get them to test  twice a week or maybe even more than  that I'm sure that the government is  going to make sure that that happens now  you can say whether that's good bad or  whatever but in my opinion they're going  to have enough tests once the season  starts to to test every player at least  twice a week the question is is the NFL  going to be ready you know to basically  act on the results of those tests in  other words if you have like three or  four guys in a week test positive that  team has got to sit down for 14 days so  that's gonna be a big question and a  couple of things here very quickly Peter  you and I were on the video conference  with the Morris Smith the NFLPA  executive director a few weeks ago and  one of my takeaways from what he said  was we are not going to agree to a  scenario where our players are taking  tests away from the general public so  even if the government decides we're  going to funnel tests to the NFL and the  NFL owners are saying bring them on the  NFLPA may put a line in the sand and say  no we what we refuse and and there's  gonna be a serious element of  negotiation here between the NFL and the  NFLPA and I think this is one of the  reasons why the NFL is treading lightly  publicly they don't want to get ahead of  themselves because they know the Union  eventually is going to have to agree to  whatever the NFL decides to do and once  they start making significant variations  like taking an entire team out of  California for training camp and/or the  full season which may become necessary  that's something the union's going to  have to agree to that's a significant  change in working conditions so I think  that that the union will have a very  strong voice in whether or not the  league is using up tests that could go  to members of the general public but I  also can't in  you to believe that based upon what  folks in the NFL believe there will be  enough testing it seems incomprehensible  now but three months is like three years  or three decades as it relates to our  understanding of the virus and  development of tests and whatnot and I  think we're gonna be stunned when we  look back on May Peter when we get to  August or September hopefully we'll be  stunned hopefully will say holy crap it  was like the Stone Age is back before  Memorial Day but I think that's what the  NFL believes and it makes it a lot  easier to test people not just twice a  week but every day before they walk into  the facility because I think that's  ultimately what they need to aspire to  do Mike the Abbott Labs right now is  developing this 15-minute tests and  right now there have been a bunch of  false negatives with that test but  you're exactly right you think two  months ago Mike two months ago yesterday  I had my last dinner out in New York  City I was shaking hands with people and  so think of what it's going to be like  two months from now three months from  now I doubt that NFL camps will open on  time I doubt that there will be a full  four games in the preseason so let's  just say the NFL we're venting this  right now just says okay all training  camps will open on August 15th  all right so wherever they're held and  if all training camps are held on August  15th which is basically three months  from this week I will be stunned if  there are not enough tests to go around  for most of the people in this country  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports

